#!RuleTest
#test FDA-SD2250 expect=violation domain=TS
#note "Row 2: TSPARMCD=CURTRT with TSVAL 'NOTADRUG' which is not an SRS preferred term of the dummy UNII dictionary -> fires. Row 1 is a valid SRS term; row 3 is another parameter (out of the CURTRT condition); row 4 has an empty TSVAL (completeness is another rule's concern -> no fire)."
#library standard=sdtmig version=3-4
#dictionaries dummy
#expectViolationCount 1
#expectViolationAt row=2 TSSEQ=2 TSVAL=NOTADRUG
dataset TS
col STUDYID  type=Char
col DOMAIN   type=Char
col TSSEQ    type=Num
col TSPARMCD type=Char
col TSVAL    type=Char
---
S01 | TS | 1 | CURTRT | ASPIRIN
S01 | TS | 2 | CURTRT | NOTADRUG
S01 | TS | 3 | AGEMAX | NOTADRUG
S01 | TS | 4 | CURTRT |
